  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 232 PM EDT Sat Oct 10 2026\n\n- Rain Mid-Week then Cooler\n\nTropical moisture will graze southeast Lower Michigan tonight \nwith low chance POPs there, then fair and warm weather expected \ninto Monday before a shortwave trough rides over the top of upper \nridging across the SE CONUS with a low pressure center tracking \nacross the central Great Lakes on Tuesday. This is followed by a \nfull latitude upper trough developing across the eastern CONUS by \nnext weekend and the potential for a stronger low on Wed-Thu\nalthough ensemble spread remains considerable on the details. \n\nAt this point it seems possible rain will be around for Wednesday\nand Thursday with sharply cooler weather for Friday and beyond.",
